  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>The quantity of electricity required in Faraday to reduce five moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For this balanced reaction, the change in oxidation number of the metal ion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Therefore one mole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> required <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> Faraday</p><p>Hence, for five mole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> required <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> Faraday.</p>",
